1
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:42,440
The strange feeling we had back then

2
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:47,720
So we walked on the arcade's guide tiles,

3
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:53,480
stepping only on the black ones.

4
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

5
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,780
but everyone has forgotten.

6
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:09,080
Pompous politicians and the
blue-eyeshadowed aunties above us,

7
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
turn that corner over there and see.

8
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:19,900
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

9
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there is Kame-ari,
well, surely Kame-ari.

10
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:33,080
Everyone, come on over to our town!

11
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:34,580
Thank you.

12
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:39,460
Hikiyori doina kankei

13
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:58,820
The Genki Engineering School guy is
fleeing toward Matsuno in a red Ferrari.

14
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:01,620
Damn, that persistent patrol car!

15
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:04,840
Shift up a gear, step on it!

16
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:05,600
Yes.

17
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:06,040
Yeah.

18
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:16,920
Boss, there's still one car chasing us.

19
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,500
What are you doing?

20
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,360
But I'm the man they called
the Red Comet of Mount Akagi,

21
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:23,820
can you keep up?

22
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:29,500
You've chased me all this way,
and there's no way I'm letting you get away!

23
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:44,120
Where on earth are we?

24
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:48,040
I think we're probably somewhere
near the border of Chiba and Ibaraki.

25
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:49,900
They're gone.

26
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,320
It hurts.

27
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,760
They're out cold, now's our chance!

28
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:09,960
Damn, we're out of gas.
Let's go, Star. Wake up!

29
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:11,920
No, no, no!

30
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:14,120
Ow

31
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:16,700
No.

32
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:19,340
Wake up, Nakagawa! They're getting away.

33
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:22,280
Forward, circle around, it's torture.

34
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:22,900
Yes.

35
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:25,780
It's torture!

36
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,120
Please!

37
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:29,520
Ugh!

38
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,360
What was that guy's deal?

39
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:53,520
Did we hit him?

40
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,880
No, we shouldn't have hit him.

41
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:57,800
Are you all right?

42
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,080
Please pull yourself together.

43
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:00,480
Where's the suspect?

44
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:03,500
I don't think he's gotten far yet.

45
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:09,700
But where on earth are we?

46
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:11,560
He'd know, surely.

47
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:15,660
Looks like an old Imperial
Japanese Army uniform.

48
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:18,460
He must have been playing
airsoft or something.

49
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:21,700
Using a replica of an
old-model gun like this!

50
00:04:22,260 --> 00:04:24,380
Get up! Get up or I'll shoot!

51
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:26,060
Bang! Like that.

52
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:30,160
It's a real gun.

53
00:04:31,560 --> 00:04:33,200
Don't you dare give back my gun.

54
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:37,300
Whoa, that was close.

55
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:39,920
After all, a gun is a police officer's soul.

56
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:42,020
Police officers.

57
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:43,340
Something stinks.

58
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:46,880
You two over there, come out slowly.

59
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:49,080
Who's he talking to?

60
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:49,780
Beats me.

61
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:52,180
No use hiding.

62
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:53,540
We can see you.

63
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,180
With that balloon-like body of yours...

64
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:59,120
That's an airbag, you idiot.

65
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,380
Is that so?

66
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:03,080
Get out of the way, airbag.

67
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:06,520
You don't even know what an airbag is,
seriously.

68
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:10,080
Approaching carelessly is dangerous, desu.

69
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:14,080
Those guys are vicious criminals
who committed violent crimes, desu.

70
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:15,120
What's that supposed to mean?

71
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:17,500
What crimes did they commit?

72
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:19,380
Speeding, desu.

73
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:22,360
How ridiculous.

74
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:24,180
This stuff is like this, like this.

75
00:05:24,180 --> 00:05:25,040
This is...

76
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:27,640
You, brother!

77
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:30,200
You used a substitution jutsu, didn't you?

78
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:31,720
By the way,

79
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:33,600
seeing through that at a glance...

80
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:35,440
who exactly are you?

81
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:39,260
I'm Senior Constable Ryotsu
of the Katsushika police box.

82
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,420
Senior Constable, sir?

83
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:44,680
I didn't realize that.
I apologize for my rudeness.

84
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:46,300
I'm

85
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:48,440
Officer Imogashira, sir!

86
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:53,700
Actually, we were the ones in this car.

87
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:54,580
Why would you

88
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:59,260
Even if you're a senior constable,
crimes can't be forgiven, you know.

89
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:02,260
We were in pursuit of a criminal.

90
00:06:02,860 --> 00:06:04,320
In pursuit of a criminal...

91
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:09,900
That's right, we came all the way from Tokyo
chasing the thief who stole 50 million yen in cash.

92
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,740
50 million yen?

93
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:19,600
You ran out in front of the car right when I had him,
and now we've lost him.

94
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:23,420
Anyone can see this car is a police car,
you know.

95
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:25,680
Look what you've done.

96
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:30,040
Then I'll die to make amends.

97
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,800
Idiot, stop!

98
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,320
Let me go, won't you.

99
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:35,920
I still have things to ask you.

100
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:38,020
We can't have you dying here.

101
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:39,160
Please.

102
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:41,960
Don't you dare commit seppuku,
that's an order from your superior!

103
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:46,900
Are you saying I should
go on living in shame?

104
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:51,000
If you catch the culprit,
you can redeem yourself too.

105
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,840
Help us out.

106
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:54,100
Y-yes.

107
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:57,180
First, please tell us where we are.

108
00:06:57,740 --> 00:07:00,440
Chiba Prefecture? Or Ibaraki Prefecture?

109
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:03,600
No, this is Doinaka Prefecture, you see.

110
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:04,900
Doinaka Prefecture?

111
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:06,980
No wonder you don't know it.

112
00:07:07,420 --> 00:07:11,520
We only made contact with the Japanese government last week,
for the first time in 55 years.

113
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:15,780
We're applying to get it
put on the map of Japan.

114
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:17,800
Hey, what do you mean by that?

115
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:19,600
I don't really understand, but

116
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:23,460
So you're saying they were
stuck like Yokoi Shoichi?

117
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:26,260
An entire prefecture, here in Japan?

118
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:29,260
Anyway, even if you bring up Yokoi or Onoda,

119
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:31,260
kids today won't get it.

120
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:32,920
Don't look at me.

121
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:35,320
Hey, just to be safe, I'll ask.

122
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:36,820
What year is it this year?

123
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:39,580
This year is Showa 75.

124
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:42,860
Showa ended more than ten years ago,
you know.

125
00:07:42,860 --> 00:07:45,080
This year is Heisei 12.

126
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:46,580
Really?

127
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:51,640
Come to think of it,
we were chasing the suspects.

128
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,900
I'll contact the station.

129
00:07:55,940 --> 00:07:58,020
No good. It seems to be broken.

130
00:07:58,700 --> 00:07:59,540
What about cell phones?

131
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:02,020
We're outside the prefecture.

132
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:04,380
I guess it can't be helped,
in a place like this.

133
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:07,320
Is there a phone somewhere?

134
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,660
There should be one if we go
back to the village, though.

135
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:11,840
Okay, lead the way.

136
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:16,660
This week is traffic enforcement week,
you know.

137
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:18,720
How many cars did you study?

138
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:21,440
No violators in 50 years.

139
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:23,780
This seems like a peaceful case.

140
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:31,100
A dog? No, that's not it.

141
00:08:31,860 --> 00:08:32,840
It's a wolf.

142
00:08:33,780 --> 00:08:36,080
It's a wolf that was supposed to be extinct.

143
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:44,060
This area's crawling with wolf packs, dasu.

144
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:45,880
What a place.

145
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:50,480
That's a crested ibis.

146
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:53,180
There's a breeding colony nearby, dasu, so.

147
00:08:53,180 --> 00:08:55,240
So many of them!

148
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:58,640
If the Environment Agency officials saw this,
they'd cry tears of joy.

149
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:03,460
Don't tell me this one's an
Iriomote wildcat or something.

150
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,020
That's just a stray cat, dasu.

151
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:07,280
I see.

152
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:11,340
I see it, dasu!

153
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:14,580
That's Podunk Prefecture,
Podunk Village, dasu!

154
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:21,240
Granny, we're borrowing the phone.

155
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:23,760
This way.

156
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:25,720
Excuse us.

157
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:28,680
You're not the kind of people we usually see around here,
are you?

158
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:31,380
They're people from Tokyo.

159
00:09:31,380 --> 00:09:33,040
Well, well, Tokyo!

160
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:38,200
This is quite an old-fashioned phone,
isn't it?

161
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:40,800
I expected it, but not this bad.

162
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:45,220
Hello, telephone exchange.

163
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:48,420
Through the exchange,
we can't get a direct line, can we?

164
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:49,900
Direct line.

165
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:52,200
That's impossible, senpai.

166
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:57,540
From the looks of it, their civilization
seems to have stopped before Showa 20.

167
00:09:58,580 --> 00:09:59,040
I see.

168
00:09:59,660 --> 00:10:01,680
Who would you like to be connected to?

169
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,560
I'd like a long-distance call to Tokyo.

170
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:06,380
Tokyo?

171
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:08,740
I'm sorry.

172
00:10:08,740 --> 00:10:11,960
We don't handle long-distance
calls at the moment, though.

173
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:15,400
What? Then this is totally useless!

174
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:17,360
That's not true, you know.

175
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:22,560
After all, people out here at the edge of the
village have been living without phone lines.

176
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:25,440
I need to make a call to Tokyo.

177
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:30,900
I hear they're currently negotiating with
the telephone company to have a line installed.

178
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:32,400
You mean NTT, right?

179
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:33,920
That's right.

180
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:36,740
Sorry, I find foreign words hard to use.

181
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:39,000
Oshimasu, senpai.

182
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:43,120
Going back down that mountain
road now is dangerous, too.

183
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:47,160
In that case, you may as well
stay at our boarding house tonight.

184
00:10:51,020 --> 00:10:52,780
What a bounty of mountain treasures!

185
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:55,160
Come on, don't hold back, dig in.

186
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:56,160
Thank you for the meal.

187
00:10:59,300 --> 00:10:59,980
It's delicious.

188
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:05,960
Hey, cucumbers used to taste like this back in the day,
didn't they?

189
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:07,840
What are you talking about?

190
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:10,420
Cucumbers have always been cucumbers.

191
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:11,720
I see.

192
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:14,500
Old-fashioned ways are good, too.

193
00:11:17,340 --> 00:11:19,580
I've been wondering about
something since earlier, but

194
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:21,680
what on earth is that?

195
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:24,820
It's my dinner I bought
at the convenience store.

196
00:11:25,220 --> 00:11:26,480
I'll give it to you.

197
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:30,180
Is this what people in Tokyo eat for dinner?

198
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,080
Please lend us some hot water.

199
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,140
We'll make it edible for you.

200
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:36,620
Here you go.

201
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:38,980
Wow, this is Chinese noodles!

202
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:40,660
How convenient, isn't it?

203
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:46,360
Do people in Tokyo eat this
kind of thing every day?

204
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:48,460
Not every day, exactly.

205
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:50,520
I eat it almost every day!

206
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:55,620
This is

207
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:56,980
cola.

208
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:59,480
It's a drink that came over after the war.

209
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:00,960
Go on, try it.

210
00:12:03,900 --> 00:12:04,420
Hey.

211
00:12:04,420 --> 00:12:11,480
Eeeeeeh! It exploded in my mouth!
That's just the kind of drink it is.

212
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,660
Is that so?

213
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:18,700
You're from Tokyo.

214
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:21,040
This is the first time I've seen
someone from outside the village.

215
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:21,800
Really?

216
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,400
Aaaaaaah!

217
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:26,740
Hey! We're not fakes, you know!

218
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:30,580
Yeah, we've never seen
anyone from Tokyo before!

219
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:34,640
Is it true that Tokyo
stays lit up all night?

220
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:37,380
Is it true that everyone
there speaks English?

221
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:40,760
Is it true that everyone dresses like this?

222
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:43,440
W-what, of course not!

223
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:47,740
Only a small number of girls in Tokyo do it.

224
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:51,140
This is how misconceptions
about Tokyo spread

225
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:55,720
I've got an idea.
Let's take a photo, it'll be fun.

226
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:58,860
There's a disposable camera here.

227
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:00,640
Photo.

228
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:03,020
Alright, I'll take it.

229
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:05,120
Say cheese!

230
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:09,420
Hey, hey, what's wrong with you?

231
00:13:09,420 --> 00:13:12,560
If you get your photo taken,
your soul gets pulled out, you know.

232
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:15,400
Come on, don't be ridiculous.

233
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:18,280
Yeah! I don't want to die yet!

234
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:27,960
B-bro...

235
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:30,020
Shoo... get away!

236
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:32,120
I can't stand this place anymore!

237
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:39,740
Good morning!

238
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:42,920
Sergeant, preparations are complete, dasu!

239
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:44,680
For what?

240
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:46,480
For the ceremony.

241
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:48,120
A ceremony?

242
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:50,220
So, that sound... are those fireworks?

243
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:58,580
What is this tank army!

244
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:00,740
It's a light armored car from
this godforsaken countryside.

245
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:03,140
So that makes them patrol cars?

246
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:06,380
They're still using wartime
tanks just as they are

247
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:19,320
What a rousing welcome!

248
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:22,200
Doesn't feel bad at all.

249
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:23,500
Thank you, thank you.

250
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:26,760
Salute Sergeant Kankichi Ryotsu!

251
00:14:30,660 --> 00:14:32,280
Sergeant Kankichi Ryotsu!

252
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:33,960
I've brought one other person with me.

253
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:39,020
Good work, Officer Imogashira.

254
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:42,060
That's an impressive number of medals!

255
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:48,920
He's definitely outranking the Chief. He might be a superintendent,
or even higher.

256
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:54,040
Welcome to Doinaka Prefecture.
I'm the chief of Doinaka Police Station.

257
00:14:54,040 --> 00:15:00,920
I'm Officer Yonesuke Omaeda. Officer?
You're the chief, so why are you an officer?

258
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:08,120
I've been a police officer for 58 years,
but I've had few chances for promotion.

259
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:14,300
After all, the only incident in these 55
years was the persimmon theft 30 years ago.

260
00:15:14,940 --> 00:15:16,080
Persimmon theft.

261
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:21,140
That case was handled by
the late Sendai station chief.

262
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:27,200
Just thinking back on Sendai's
achievements then brings tears to my eyes.

263
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:32,000
Thanks to that achievement,
Sendai was promoted to sergeant,

264
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:36,580
but since then nothing has happened,
so everyone's still a patrolman.

265
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:51,460
Well then, this is the 10-year service medal.
Here are the 15-year and 20-year ones, and this one is for runner-up in the summer festival endurance contest, the 25-year medal.

266
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:54,460
Participating in the prefectural
sports festival counts too.

267
00:16:02,660 --> 00:16:04,920
Why was that flock of birds

268
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:06,060
Guess I'll drive, then.

269
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:09,780
Let's get out of these
mountains and skip town somewhere.

270
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:11,860
I hear a car's engine.

271
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:14,280
I don't care what kind of vehicle it is.

272
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:15,920
We're taking that car!

273
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:17,260
Stop!

274
00:16:19,380 --> 00:16:21,380
What an odd vehicle.

275
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:23,020
It's a reckless, idiotic car!

276
00:16:27,780 --> 00:16:48,180
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

277
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:50,980
I was on my way to tend the fields,
wasn't I?

278
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:53,520
The biggest incident in thirty years!

279
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:56,880
It must be the cash
robbers we've been chasing!

280
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:58,520
Yes, there's no doubt about it.

281
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:04,660
Senior Constable, you hold the highest rank here.
Your orders?

282
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:08,620
Got it! All patrol cars, deploy!

283
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:17,360
You there, Officer!
The suspects' predicted route is -

284
00:17:18,580 --> 00:17:21,580
They say the road ahead
is also a normal route.

285
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:24,560
Right, all units, ambush them there!

286
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:31,980
Damn it, where on earth are we?

287
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:33,940
It's not even on the map!

288
00:17:34,940 --> 00:17:36,920
Bro, there's a car ahead!

289
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:39,460
Idiot, just plow right through it!

290
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:41,100
We're a patrol car, you know!

291
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:42,000
But that's -

292
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:43,900
So what?

293
00:17:49,540 --> 00:17:51,160
Alright, here they come.

294
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:53,320
Damn it, get out of the way!

295
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:56,280
Is this a through road?

296
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:57,900
You've done it now.

297
00:17:57,900 --> 00:17:59,100
Return fire!

298
00:17:59,100 --> 00:18:01,440
Shoot, shoot, keep shooting!

299
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:13,920
Those Nasca tanks are

300
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:15,100
maybe

301
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:18,200
we may have wandered into
an SDF training ground.

302
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:24,140
No! They're aiming at us!

303
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:26,240
We've been shot! We've been shot!

304
00:18:28,860 --> 00:18:30,460
Got it! A motorbike!

305
00:18:34,260 --> 00:18:36,700
Damn! The culprits took the motorbike!

306
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:39,720
That's the only large
vehicle in the village.

307
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:41,660
Bring out the quick-firing tank.

308
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:44,840
Damn! Slow tanks can't catch up!

309
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:46,460
No need to worry.

310
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:49,540
The Toyoda prefectural police also has an air police unit,
you know.

311
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:51,280
Air police unit.

312
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,960
Hien, Hayabusa, Hayate.

313
00:18:55,780 --> 00:18:56,980
Raiden, Shiden-Kai.

314
00:18:56,980 --> 00:18:58,420
And the Zero.

315
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:01,320
Aren't they all planes from the war?

316
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:04,200
If plane buffs saw this, they'd go wild.

317
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:05,620
Sergeant.

318
00:19:05,620 --> 00:19:07,040
Which one are we taking?

319
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:09,200
I'm going with the Zero, of course.

320
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:15,780
They went this way, the bastards!

321
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:17,260
Sergeant!

322
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:19,640
Bottom left, along the crosshairs!

323
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:20,500
What?

324
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:23,480
That one?

325
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:26,360
Right, commence the attack!

326
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:27,120
Yes.

327
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:32,840
Bro!

328
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:37,360
Get ready to die!

329
00:19:44,520 --> 00:19:46,060
Hey, that's a Zero, right?

330
00:19:46,060 --> 00:19:47,540
Why is there a Zero here?

331
00:19:47,540 --> 00:19:49,680
Like hell I'm dying here!

332
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:54,680
Anyway, let's get out of here

333
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:04,800
I figured they'd run this way,
so I sent the Water Police out too!

334
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:07,360
I never knew there was
a battleship like that!

335
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:08,660
What a place this is!

336
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:13,180
I saw it... was that a depth-charge sabre?

337
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:23,060
Screw this life.

338
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:28,120
Hey, it's too early to give up!

339
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:34,560
Siphoning gas from a busted patrol car,
that's just like you, big brother!

340
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:38,600
Ride this thing and
we've got nothing to fear!

341
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,800
Still no sign of the suspects?

342
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:47,980
Sir, we still haven't found them!

343
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:50,360
I'm a senior constable, you know!

344
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:54,040
Found the suspects' car near the checkpoint!

345
00:20:54,040 --> 00:20:57,020
They're fleeing at an unbelievable speed!

346
00:20:57,580 --> 00:20:59,920
It's the Ferrari they were driving at first.

347
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:01,760
It can hit 300 kilometers an hour, you know.

348
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,860
At this rate, they're going to get away!

349
00:21:03,860 --> 00:21:05,560
We have no choice.

350
00:21:05,560 --> 00:21:07,740
Looks like we have to bring that out.

351
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:21,920
This is the Toyonaka Police
Railway Unit's train cannon, dasu.

352
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:22,940
No way, that's crazy.

353
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:28,100
Come on, Sergeant, give the order!

354
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:32,160
Screw it, fire! Fire!

355
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:34,900
Roger, dasu.
Preparing the train cannon to fire.

356
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:35,080
Ready!

357
00:21:35,620 --> 00:21:37,200
Far south-southwest!

358
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:38,920
Maru-Seven-Two-Maru!

359
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:41,960
Distance 22.25 km!

360
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:46,740
North-northeast wind! Wind force 2!

361
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:51,200
Target acquired! Error correction!
Right point two degrees!

362
00:21:53,920 --> 00:21:55,780
Firing in ten seconds!

363
00:21:57,100 --> 00:22:02,360
6! 5! 4! 3! 2! 1!

364
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:03,660
Fire!

365
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:10,380
Get over this mountain and we're
done with this ridiculous village!

366
00:22:16,020 --> 00:22:18,080
Yay! What a great shot!

367
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:24,420
I can't take this anymore.
Please, just arrest them normally.

368
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:27,020
Yeah! Great shot!

369
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:30,920
Bajoi! Bajoi! Bajoi!

370
00:22:30,920 --> 00:22:33,960
Somehow I'm starting to
feel sorry for the criminals.

371
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:35,180
Indeed.

372
00:22:37,160 --> 00:22:38,740
I can't believe it.

373
00:22:38,740 --> 00:22:40,640
That there's a police station like that.

374
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:43,880
Well, we don't want to believe it either.

375
00:22:45,020 --> 00:22:47,540
But Kei-chan wouldn't lie.

376
00:22:47,540 --> 00:22:50,500
And the criminals we caught
are saying the same thing.

377
00:22:50,500 --> 00:22:54,440
Honestly,
this is like a Twilight Zone episode.

378
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:55,800
Ryotsu!

379
00:22:55,800 --> 00:22:59,580
You wrote something about the Doinaka police box in your report,
didn't you?

380
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:02,620
I'm not saying you have
to believe it, but...

381
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:07,080
We've got a radio call from Officer
Imogashira at that Doinaka police box.

382
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:08,960
From Imogashira?

383
00:23:10,980 --> 00:23:13,080
This is Ryotsu of Katsushika Station.

384
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:14,360
Sergeant.

385
00:23:14,840 --> 00:23:17,020
Imogashira, what on earth is going on?

386
00:23:17,020 --> 00:23:19,080
Another violent crime has

387
00:23:19,860 --> 00:23:21,240
a violent crime, I tell you!

388
00:23:21,860 --> 00:23:23,120
It's a persimmon thief, dasu.

389
00:23:24,720 --> 00:23:28,200
The suspect crossed the prefectural
border and is heading toward Tokyo, dasu.

390
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:31,260
We're pursuing with all
our strength too, dasu.

391
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:33,280
We ask for your cooperation, dasu.

392
00:23:33,760 --> 00:23:35,640
With all our strength, you say?

393
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:37,180
No way.

394
00:23:42,340 --> 00:23:43,560
We won't let them get away, dasu.

395
00:23:43,560 --> 00:23:45,220
This Kokoaddohan!

396
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:54,780
All units, ready to fire in unison!

397
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:55,780
Fire!

398
00:24:27,060 --> 00:24:33,320
Making do with one hand,
beef bowl with extra sauce on a cloudy day.

399
00:24:33,900 --> 00:24:40,280
Overtime stress and irritation
melt away with ylang-ylang.

400
00:24:43,660 --> 00:24:50,060
Every day's no problem, after a hot shower.

401
00:24:50,060 --> 00:24:56,660
Every day's no problem,
recharged with a sleep pillow.

402
00:24:59,820 --> 00:25:06,280
Every day's no problem, I love who I am.

403
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:13,080
Every day's no problem,
Monday with hearts flying around.

404
00:25:13,080 --> 00:25:16,420
Anten, anten, no problem.

405
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:24,380
So Honda's childhood friend runs a circus?

406
00:25:24,380 --> 00:25:26,820
I used to come see it all
the time when I was a kid.

407
00:25:27,620 --> 00:25:30,440
Apparently the circus is about
to be taken to settle a debt.

408
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:33,960
Leave it to me, I'll sort it out somehow.

409
00:25:34,540 --> 00:25:37,860
Next time, Circus Symphony, see you then.

410
00:25:38,700 --> 00:25:40,820
That place is Kameari-ry.

411
00:25:41,940 --> 00:25:44,980
Well, surely Kameari-ry.

412
00:25:44,980 --> 00:25:49,180
Everyone, come on over to our town!

413
00:25:50,100 --> 00:25:50,760
Thank you.

